WEBVTT

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:38.360
<i>The light sings</i>

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:46.970
<i>Chasing the floating clouds</i>

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.770
<i>Little cricket</i>

00:01:54.080 --> 00:02:00.530
<i>It jumps and plays on the green grass</i>

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:10.310
<i>Flying over the babbling brooks</i>

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.700
<i>Glistening in the light</i>

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:32.370
<i>The setting sun leads me with its long shadow</i>

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.920
Thank you.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.570
The battles with the aliens

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.790
have demonstrated the EX-1
can be used effectively as a weapon.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:12.120
Harriet has also become more manageable,

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:16.750
and through her, we can
control the EX-1 more efficiently.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:22.500
So from now on, we should proceed
with the EX-1 making initial contact...

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.220
...then deploying the SARGs for a joint assault.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.930
That is the plan the commander
and I formulated.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.890
A joint assault with the EX-1, eh?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.980
So our rookie with the wild arm
has finally come into his own.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:37.690
And speaking of rookies...

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.180
...someone else is turning into a team player.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.620
Now that you mention it...

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.950
The time with the type M-1...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.760
And the time with the type G-4...

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.410
It was Lt. Soma and the EX-1's
teamwork that beat the aliens.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.630
An unlikely pair like Abbot and Costello.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:56.770
No!

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.330
More pictures today?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.570
Yup.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.230
Want to read the rest of the picture book?

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:10.330
Well, do you want to read it...together?

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:15.970
But...

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.610
Something wrong?

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.310
But...

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.410
It's almost...

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:22.010
Almost what?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.120
Time for me to go home...

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.160
...and cook dinner together!

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.490
See you later, Mr. Fairy!

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.240
I'm used to being alone.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.680
Where's Lt. Soma?

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.690
At the SARG compound.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:02.630
Making some electrical repairs.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.190
Since when is he so conscientious?

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.630
Now all the SARGs but
number four will be ready.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.210
She's really charmed that kid.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:18.180
Don't be too sure.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.400
I wouldn't have thought it...

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.640
...but it looks like her maternal instincts...

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.380
...have kicked in again.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.960
Yes?

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.390
Understood.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:38.990
I'll be there right away.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.610
We received those this morning.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.380
Along with a very threatening letter.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:03.940
This isn't the first time...

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.930
...the mass media's been close
to blowing the whistle on the EX-1.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:13.800
Luckily, Section 9 has always
been able to plug the leaks.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.770
But we have absolutely
no idea who sent this note.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.200
We don't know who to plug.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.930
We don't know the motivation,

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:26.760
but it's possible that some
insider is leaking information.

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:33.380
Section 9 is trying to trace the letter,
but don't expect too much.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:38.250
If the public finds out we're using
this alien patchwork, it won't be good.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:43.920
It'll damage civilian trust in both
Funeral and the military as a whole.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.330
Once that happens, it'll be too late.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:51.750
We've got to find a way to prevent
that kind of publicity to the military.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.470
So that's that.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.070
If the EX-1 goes out of control
even for the slightest amount of time,

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:03.780
or if there is even a 1 percent probability
of it causing harm to civilians,

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:06.620
take it down by force.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:11.350
The insurance...are you saying
to use the thermonuclear warhead?

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:14.080
The decision is yours.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.600
Do you mind if I ask you a question?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.650
Sure...

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:40.420
I've wondered about this for a long time.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:44.580
Why was I, a woman,
chosen to be the head of Funeral?

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.220
An ulterior motive?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.180
I hadn't really thought it through, no.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:57.830
We lost all our capable men to
the first war, to answer your question.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:12.810
The choice was a less competent man
and a capable woman.

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:16.480
So I'm not a decoration.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:18.580
Am I free to conclude that?

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.450
Enough stupid questions.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.350
I retire in two years.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.990
Don't do anything to ruin
my rose garden dream.

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.270
So one of us might be a traitor?

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.350
It’s just speculation.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.670
Could it be a spy for someone with a grudge?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:38.370
Or just...

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.840
...some nuts with strange ideas about aliens.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.470
In any event...

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:48.680
...now we can't put the EX-1 on
the mound until the game's underway.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:51.850
So we're going back to the old formation.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:56.090
These military brass are
missing the big picture.

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:02.010
They'll sacrifice the best thing we
have just to cover their own asses.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.740
We can minimize the loss.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:13.610
I've analyzed the EX-1's individual
parts and how they each move.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.230
If it comes to that...

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:18.240
...the Excalibur can take his head.

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.020
See you next Wednesday.

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.180
You bet.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.290
And don't forget the magazine.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.690
Aye aye, sir.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.150
The EX-1 has broken out of jail.
Repeat.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.900
The EX-1 has broken out of jail.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.300
Where's Harriet?

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.550
I'm checking.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.580
She's in your private residence.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.130
What's the EX-1's position?

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:15.440
At 007.012.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:18.760
Running north by northeast
at 60 km per hour.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.240
SARGs 1, 3, and 5, deploy.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.650
Go get the EX-1.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.780
Lt. Harris, stay here.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:29.820
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:35.020
Shouldn't we bring Harriet along?

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:39.150
Until we know why he's escaped,
there's no reason to endanger her.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:46.040
This is...

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.400
We'll catch the EX-1!

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:27.460
Shoot!

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:32.870
Malfunction in firing liquid injection?

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.910
What are those mechanics doing?

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.020
Guenevere, fall back.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.820
No point if you can't fire.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:41.020
Understood.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.330
I thought he was trained, and he runs loose.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.330
He's such a troublesome pet!

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:51.890
Lt. Soma, what's wrong?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.100
A problem with my auto balancer.

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:57.100
Get control of it!

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.610
I'm trying to.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:03.280
Must be because we just changed
the circuits.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:04.880
Just clear back.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:05.920
Yes, sir.

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:11.500
Lieutenant!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:12.620
Can't help it.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.180
Better let me take care of him.

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:18.550
Let me back you up if
your machine isn't working.

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:21.100
No, you shouldn't risk it.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.230
You should go back, Lieutenant.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.270
It's all going as planned.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:05.640
Your existence is the only miscalculation.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:33.440
If only I hadn't shown up to help...

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:41.000
If only I stopped Maki,
that wouldn't have happened...

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.440
You really are ugly.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.820
You’re just a heap of scars!

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.850
Go back!

00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:57.390
Back to being junk!

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.010
Maki...

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.050
Give her...

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.420
...back to me.

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:51.040
What's wrong?

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.510
You hate me?

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:58.450
Me, the one who called
you out of your grave?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.190
Well then, hit me!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.330
Come on, do it!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.130
Come get me!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.890
Why...

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.090
...do you...

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:47.030
Lt. Soma, keep doing what you're doing.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.370
We found out why the EX-1 is running.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.480
He's locked on to Harriet's personal signal.

00:16:52.810 --> 00:16:56.210
We've sent the captain to find out
where it's coming from.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:06.780
Harriet is going over there, too.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.620
The situation is going fine.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:10.320
Please, continue for a while.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:14.970
I'm finished playing.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:24.900
Go back to the morgue!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.650
I...

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.390
...hate you!

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.490
That's it.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.800
Mr. Fairy, you can’t just go
outside without telling anyone!

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.360
Lt. Soma, you still alive?

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:02.990
Lt. Soma?

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:07.040
Lt. Soma, answer me!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:25.590
Ah, humans who don't know gratitude.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.870
They're the worst monsters of all.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:29.860
The worst.

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.330
You're the absolute worst.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.540
You broke the terms of our contract
without permission.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.270
Contemptible, if it weren't so amusing.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:46.870
You hate Frank, but he doesn't even
acknowledge you as an enemy.

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.950
All he cares about is her.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.420
Right, little Harriet?

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:05.960
You should be ashamed.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.490
You can't do such bad things.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:11.800
The driver of that truck
lost his job because of this.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.960
You're a bad boy...

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.170
...so I should tell the teacher.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.940
If you can't even take on
a little guy like me...

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.470
...how will you ever get
your revenge on Frank?

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.590
How weak.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.250
You’re just a weakling...

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:40.260
...Takuto Kaneshiro.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.990
I'm not Takuto!

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:45.000
I'm going to tell you something.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:50.580
We can always send Ryu Soma
2 and 3 if you don't do your job.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.070
That's right.

00:21:52.140 --> 00:21:56.910
Just like when we sent you
after the late pilot of SARG 2.

00:21:56.980 --> 00:21:58.450
Then the accident was...

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.810
What are you talking about?

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:07.890
The best thing to do is take
advantage of others' hard times.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:35.000
Malice and Betrayal

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:38.920
Corrupted now by despair, he cries out...

00:22:38.920 --> 00:22:41.860
..."I've thrown down that rusty spear."

00:22:43.330 --> 00:22:46.420
And with it, all bad dreams fall to the ground.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:49.270
Next time,
Betrayal and Despair.
